{"name":"Honeysweet","hex":"#e9cfc8","fetched":"2026-10-12","looked":{"definitions":[{"term":"honeysweet","whole":true,"parts":[{"part":"Noun","definitions":["Term of endearment."]}],"link":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/honeysweet"}],"entries":[{"title":"Tidestromia","blocks":[{"text":"Tidestromia is a genus with about six or seven species of annual or subshrub perennial plants native to desert and semi-arid regions of the western United States, Mexico and tropical America in the family Amaranthaceae. A common name of some species is honeysweet. The stems are reddish and contrast conspicuously with the silvery leaves. This genus is named for the botanist Ivar Tidestrom."}],"image":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/4/4b/Tidestromia_lanuginosa.jpg/330px-Tidestromia_lanuginosa.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=api&utm_content=thumbnail","link":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Tidestromia","wikidata":"Q7800866"}],"images":[],"sounds":{},"pictures":[{"title":"Werner's nomenclature of colours greys","image":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/e/e6/Werner%27s_nomenclature_of_colours_greys.jpg/500px-Werner%27s_nomenclature_of_colours_greys.jpg","ratio":0.794047619047619,"link":"https://commons.wikimedia.org/wiki/File:Werner%27s_nomenclature_of_colours_greys.jpg","share":0.845625},{"title":"Grey heron (00129p)","image":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/6/64/Grey_heron_%2800129p%29.jpg/500px-Grey_heron_%2800129p%29.jpg","ratio":0.8691693290734824,"link":"https://commons.wikimedia.org/wiki/File:Grey_heron_(00129p).jpg","share":0.515625},{"title":"Near Ryan Draw - Flickr - aspidoscelis","image":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/4/45/Near_Ryan_Draw_-_Flickr_-_aspidoscelis.jpg/500px-Near_Ryan_Draw_-_Flickr_-_aspidoscelis.jpg","ratio":1.5,"link":"https://commons.wikimedia.org/wiki/File:Near_Ryan_Draw_-_Flickr_-_aspidoscelis.jpg","share":0.179375},{"title":"East-northeast of Little Black Mountain -